   "state": "normal",
   "title": "Volatility",
   "text": "The VIX is 15.1, against a ten-year median of 16.9. It is the S&P 500 options market's price for the next 30 days' swings. Momentum strategies have historically suffered their sharpest losses in rebounds after high-volatility declines (Daniel & Moskowitz 2016), which is why this screener already cuts momentum's weight when the universe is turbulent and raises it when calm."
  },
